A prophet in the reign of Rehoboam (1 Kings 12:22-24).","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"solomon_2762","name":"Solomon","also":"Jedidiah","summary":"Peaceful, (Heb. Shelomoh), David’s second son by Bathsheba, i.e., the first after their legal marriage (2 Sam. 12). He was probably born about B.C. 1035 (1 Chr. 22:5; 29:1).","verses":273,"father":"David","mother":"Bathsheba","v":[3,17]},{"id":"jeroboam_872","name":"Jeroboam","also":"","summary":"The son of Nebat (1 Kings 11:26-39), “an Ephrathite,” the first king of the ten tribes, over whom he reigned twenty-two years (B.C. 976-945).","verses":81,"father":"Nebat","mother":"Zeruah","v":[4,14]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[17,18]},{"id":"jesse_903","name":"Jesse","also":"","summary":"Firm, or a gift, a son of Obed, the son of Boaz and Ruth (Ruth 4:17, 22; Matt. 1:5, 6; Luke 3:32). He was the father of eight sons, the youngest of whom was David (1 Sam. 17:12).","verses":44,"father":"Obed","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"eliab_1075","name":"Eliab","also":"","summary":"Son of Kohath.","verses":5,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"abihail_31","name":"Abihail","also":"","summary":"The second wife of King Rehoboam (2 Chr. 11:18), a descendant of Eliab, David’s eldest brother.","verses":1,"father":"Eliab","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"jerimoth_869","name":"Jerimoth","also":"","summary":"One of David’s sons (2 Chr. 11:18).","verses":1,"father":"David","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"mahalath_1888","name":"Mahalath","also":"","summary":"The daughter of Jerimoth, who was one of David’s sons.","verses":1,"father":"Jerimoth","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"jeush_1603","name":"Jeush","also":"","summary":"One of the three sons of Rehoboam (2 Chr. 11:19).","verses":1,"father":"Rehoboam","mother":"Abihail","v":[19]},{"id":"shamariah_2531","name":"Shamariah","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"Rehoboam","mother":"Abihail","v":[19]},{"id":"zaham_2980","name":"Zaham","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"Rehoboam","mother":"Abihail","v":[19]},{"id":"absalom_59","name":"Absalom","also":"Abishalom","summary":"Father of peace; i.e., “peaceful” David’s son by Maacah (2 Sam. 3:3; comp. 1 Kings 1:6). He was noted for his personal beauty and for the extra-ordinary profusion of the hair of his head (2 Sam. 14:25,26).","verses":91,"father":"David","mother":"Maacah","v":[20,21]},{"id":"abijah_38","name":"Abijah","also":"Abijam, Abia","summary":"The son of Rehoboam, whom he succeeded on the throne of Judah (1 Chr. 3:10). He is also called Abijam (1 Kings 14:31; 15:1-8). He began his three years’ reign (2 Chr. 12:16; 13:1, 2) with a strenuous but unsuccessful effort to bring back the ten tribes to their allegiance.","verses":20,"father":"Rehoboam","mother":"Maachah","v":[20,22]},{"id":"maachah_1841","name":"Maachah","also":"Michaiah","summary":"The daughter of Abishalom (called Absalom, 2 Chr. 11:20-22), the third wife of Rehoboam, and mother of Abijam (1 Kings 15:2). She is called “Michaiah the daughter of Uriel,” who was the husband of Absalom’s daughter Tamar (2 Chr. 13:2).","verses":8,"father":"Uriel","mother":"Tamar","v":[20,21,22]},{"id":"attai_365","name":"Attai","also":"","summary":"Son of Rehoboam.","verses":1,"father":"Rehoboam","mother":"Maachah","v":[20]},{"id":"shelomith_2610","name":"Shelomith","also":"","summary":"Son of Josiphiah.","verses":1,"father":"Rehoboam","mother":"Maachah","v":[20]},{"id":"ziza_3098","name":"Ziza","also":"","summary":"A son of Rehoboam (2 Chr. 11:20).","verses":1,"father":"Rehoboam","mother":"Maachah","v":[20]}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[1,5,14,16]},{"id":"judah-southern_1281","name":"Judah (Southern)","kind":"Region","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Added from Digital Manna places-1257 (LPF sync 2026-10-13)","verses":8,"v":[5]},{"id":"bethlehem_218","name":"Bethlehem","kind":"City","lat":31.70431,"lon":35.20746,"summary":"A city in the “hill country” of Judah. It was originally called Ephrath (Gen. 35:16, 19; 48:7; Ruth 4:11). It was also called Beth-lehem Ephratah (Micah 5:2), Beth-lehem-judah (1 Sam. 17:12), and “the city of David” (Luke 2:4).","verses":32,"v":[6]},{"id":"etam_416","name":"Etam","kind":"City","lat":31.68646,"lon":35.17474,"summary":"A city of Judah, fortified by Rehoboam (2 Chr. 11:6). It was near Bethlehem and Tekoah, and some distance apparently to the north of (1). It seems to have been in the district called Nephtoah (or Netophah), where were the sources of the water from which Solomon’s gardens and pleasure-grounds and pools, as well as Bethlehem and the temple, were supplied.","verses":1,"v":[6]},{"id":"tekoa_1142","name":"Tekoa","kind":"Settlement","lat":31.63609,"lon":35.21535,"summary":"Pitching of tents; fastening down, a town of Judah, about 12 miles south of Jerusalem, and visible from the city. From this place Joab procured a “wise woman,” who pretended to be in great affliction, and skilfully made her case known to David.","verses":7,"v":[6]},{"id":"adullam_31","name":"Adullam","kind":"City","lat":31.65735,"lon":34.99924,"summary":"One of the royal cities of the Canaanites, now ‘Aid-el-ma (Josh. 12:15; 15:35). It stood on the old Roman road in the valley of Elah, which was the scene of David’s memorable victory over Goliath (1 Sam. 17:2), and not far from Gath.","verses":8,"v":[7]},{"id":"beth-zur_242","name":"Beth-zur","kind":"Settlement","lat":31.59611,"lon":35.10262,"summary":"","verses":3,"v":[7]},{"id":"soco_1104","name":"Soco","kind":"","lat":31.68123,"lon":34.9764,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[7]},{"id":"gath_442","name":"Gath","kind":"City","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"A wine-vat, one of the five royal cities of the Philistines (Josh. 13:3) on which the ark brought calamity (1 Sam. 5:8, 9; 6:17). It was famous also as being the birthplace or residence of Goliath (1 Sam. 17:4).","verses":32,"v":[8]},{"id":"mareshah_767","name":"Mareshah","kind":"City","lat":31.59296,"lon":34.89824,"summary":"Possession, a city in the plain of Judah (John. 15:44). Here Asa defeated Zerah the Ethiopian (2 Chr. 14:9, 10).","verses":6,"v":[8]},{"id":"ziph_1266","name":"Ziph","kind":"City","lat":31.47825,"lon":35.14051,"summary":"A city in the mountains of Judah (Josh. 15:55), identified with the uninhabited ruins of Tell ez-Zif, about 5 miles south-east of Hebron.","verses":6,"v":[8]},{"id":"adoraim_28","name":"Adoraim","kind":"","lat":31.51667,"lon":34.98333,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[9]},{"id":"azekah_128","name":"Azekah","kind":"City","lat":31.70064,"lon":34.93619,"summary":"Dug over, a town in the Shephelah or low hills of Judah (Josh. 15:35), where the five confederated Amoritish kings were defeated by Joshua and their army destroyed by a hailstrom (10:10, 11).","verses":7,"v":[9]},{"id":"lachish_711","name":"Lachish","kind":"City","lat":31.56522,"lon":34.84907,"summary":"Impregnable, a royal Canaanitish city in the Shephelah, or maritime plain of Palestine (Josh. 10:3, 5; 12:11). It was taken and destroyed by the Israelites (Josh. 10:31-33).","verses":22,"v":[9]},{"id":"aijalon_40","name":"Aijalon","kind":"City","lat":31.84488,"lon":35.03127,"summary":"A city in the tribe of Zebulun (Judg. 12:12), the modern Jalun, three miles north of Cabul.","verses":9,"v":[10]},{"id":"hebron_551","name":"Hebron","kind":"City","lat":31.52435,"lon":35.10854,"summary":"A city in the south end of the valley of Eshcol, about midway between Jerusalem and Beersheba, from which it is distant about 20 miles in a straight line.","verses":56,"v":[10]},{"id":"zorah_1275","name":"Zorah","kind":"City","lat":31.76214,"lon":34.96932,"summary":"Place of wasps, a town in the low country of Judah, afterwards given to Dan (Josh. 19:41; Judg. 18:2), probably the same as Zoreah (Josh. 15:33).","verses":9,"v":[10]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[7346,7346,935,3389,3389,6950,6950,1004,1004,3063,3063,1144,1144,977,4421,3898,5973,3478,7725,7725,4467,4467,7346,7346],[1697,1697,1697,3068,3068,3068,1961,413,8098,376,376,430,430],[559,7346,1121,8010,8010,4428,3063,3063,413,3605,3478,3478,3063,3063,1144,1144],[3541,3541,3541,3541,3068,3068,559,3808,3808,3808,5927,5927,5927,3898,3898,5973,251,251,376,7725,7725,7725,7725,1004,3588,2088,1961,854,854,8085,8085,8085,1697,1697,1697,3068,3068,3068,7725,7725,7725,1980,1980,413,3379],[7346,3427,3389,3389,1129,1129,1129,1129,5892,4692,4692,3063,3063],[1129,1129,1129,1035,5862,8620],[1049,7755,5725],[1661,4762,2128],[115,3923,5825],[6881,357,2275,2275,4694,4694,5892,3063,3063,1144,1144],[2388,2388,4694,4694,5414,5414,5057,0,0,214,214,3978,3978,8081,3196,3196],[6793,6793,6793,6793,7420,7420,3605,3605,5892,5892,2388,2388,2388,7235,3063,3063,1144,1144,1961,0,0],[3548,3548,3548,3881,3881,834,3605,1366,1366,3605,3478,3320,5921,5921],[3588,3881,3881,5800,4054,4054,272,272,272,1980,1980,3063,3063,3389,3389,3588,3379,1121,1121,1121,2186,2186,2186,3547,3547,3068,3068,3068],[5975,5975,5975,0,0,3548,1116,1116,1116,1116,8163,8163,8163,8163,8163,5695,5695,5695,6213,6213,6213],[3605,3605,3605,7626,3478,3478,5414,5414,5414,3824,3824,1245,1245,3068,3068,3478,430,935,935,935,3389,3389,2076,2076,3068,3068,3068,430,430,1,1,1],[2388,2388,2388,4438,4438,3063,3063,553,553,7346,1121,8010,8010,7969,7969,8141,3588,1980,1980,7969,7969,8141,1870,1870,1870,1732,1732,8010,8010],[7346,7346,3947,4258,1121,1121,1121,1121,1732,1732,1121,3406,32,32,32,1323,1323,3448,3448,1121,446],[3205,3205,1121,0,0,3266,8114,2093,2093],[310,310,3947,3947,4601,1323,53,53,3205,3205,3205,0,0,29,6262,212